Cell["\<\
The numbers of the figures compared with the data files of the original \
program\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"107fa5f7-5df2-4c80-ad93-3f3fc75129de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The original program t2_fields wrote the numbers of its two figures into \
three data files: t2_dispersion_lattice.csv (the 48 points of Figure 1: for \
",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "LL", "W"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], 
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "4a89bada-9742-433a-b54e-5d91c6cffc63"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3969ef73-cea5-457c-816a-bc33b9060fe7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "LL", "W"], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], 
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "ca41234e-3b11-4dc0-b0cd-7ac4e3493142"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d034d185-271e-4fa1-8983-bef36a931e5a"],
 " and each of the 24 momenta, the largest eigenvalue of the lattice \
operator), t2_dispersion_curves.csv (the 802 points of the curves of Figure \
1: for ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "LL", "W"], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], 
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "a2c9a934-352a-4d4e-823e-d21a95f8b4d9"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a4f36e00-6c1e-4533-ae4d-46faa2824a6c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "LL", "W"], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], 
    TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
   "2d2b4903-38b4-4679-a565-eacf400eccea"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "912fa22a-4900-4b5a-92dd-0c66c67f3c16"],
 " and each of 401 momenta, the continuum energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "LL"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"403e4343-2f5a-42ca-b831-d448489a8c49"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"91cccdba-f2bd-4b54-8050-f982019247be"],
 " and the formula of ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "LL", "lat"], TraditionalForm]], 
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"7fc8f923-ad82-4e9a-bf72-84efbb5a86cc"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e179fc6f-f1da-4ece-91f9-2006d12c7b65"],
 ") and t2_rk4_stability.csv (the 641 values of the modulus of the RK4 factor \
of Figure 2, for ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{"|", 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "|", "\[LongEqual]", "0", ",", "0.005", ",", 
     "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "3.2"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"a6945845-df9e-4e3f-b320-443ab0f173db"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f7b141b9-e0cb-4c9c-8cb4-faac3b844336"],
 "). The files print the numbers with 10 decimals (12 for the RK4 factor). \
The next cell contains every number of the three files, copied without \
change, so that the notebook stays complete; the check after it compares them \
with the lists ",
 StyleBox["points",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["curves",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["rkData",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " computed above, row by row and column by column. Because the files are \
rounded, deviations up to half a unit of the last printed decimal, ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{"5", "\[Cross]", 
     SuperscriptBox["10", 
      RowBox[{"-", "11"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"9622c793-7f8b-4028-b2cf-86e2ed068658"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a9b14764-175b-4610-8d2d-62f69c8c5105"],
 " (and ",
 Cell[BoxData[Cell[BoxData[
   FormBox[
    RowBox[{"5", "\[Cross]", 
     SuperscriptBox["10", 
      RowBox[{"-", "13"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
   ExpressionUUID->"a173a56c-cb81-4779-9cc0-88c6cd6a44dd"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0a1cb9b7-aa1a-47c7-addd-aac271fc07b6"],
 "), are expected; larger deviations would mean that the rewritten programs \
compute different numbers."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d01df2b-6e80-465a-b519-e6617b674a3f"],

